# A shell script or a python module checked out with CRLF does not run: the
# kernel reads \r as part of the interpreter path. Windows needs these LF even
# in a Windows checkout, so they are pinned rather than left to core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
# cmd.exe is the one interpreter that needs its own line ending: a label or a
# goto in an LF batch file can be read wrong. PowerShell reads LF, so .ps1 is
# left alone with everything else.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git neither converts them nor tries to diff them.
*.dic binary
*.onnx binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ogg binary
